          ],
          "text": "You came in after a road traffic collision at around 40mph as a restrained driver.\n\nThe team found:\n- A broken left shin bone (closed left tibial shaft fracture)\n- A small tear to your spleen (grade II splenic laceration)\n- Broken ribs on the left, ribs 7 to 9, with a small collection of blood near your lung (haemothorax)\n- Small fractures to a bone in your lower back (undisplaced L1 transverse process fractures)"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.1",
          "heading": "what_we_did",
          "source_ids": [
            "sections.2",
            "sections.3"
          ],
          "text": "You were cared for by several specialist teams.\n\nFor your broken shin bone:\n- On day 2 (13/05), surgeons fixed the bone with a nail inserted into the shin (intramedullary nail left tibia)\n\nFor your spleen:\n- Scans and blood tests were done to monitor it\n- It was managed without an operation\n- By day 2 your observations and blood results were stable\n- A repeat scan on day 4 (15/05) showed the spleen was improving\n\nFor your ribs and blood near your lung:\n- A drain was put into your chest to remove the blood\n- By day 2 (13/05) the drain was working and your lung was re-expanding\n- The drain was removed on day 4 (15/05)\n- A chest X-ray on day 4 (15/05) was satisfactory after the drain was removed\n\nOn day 4 (15/05) you started moving around with the physiotherapy team, putting some weight on your left leg as guided by the orthopaedic team."
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.2",
          "heading": "medicines",
          "source_ids": [],
          "text": "{{MEDICATIONS}}"
        },
        {
          "section_id": "c_sections.3",
          "heading": "next_steps",
          "source_ids": [
